07-21","text":"Received in the Senate. Read twice. Placed on Senate Legislative Calendar under General Orders. Calendar No. 463."},"laws":[],"number":"4348","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Health","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"S000522","district":4,"fullName":"Rep. Smith, Christopher H. [R-NJ-4]","party":"R","state":"NJ"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2026-07-02","actionDesc":"Reported to House","text":"<p>This bill reauthorizes through FY2030 activities of the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention to address vector-borne diseases (e.g., diseases spread by bites from ticks or mosquitoes). These activities include (1) a national strategy, (2) grants for regional centers of excellence, and (3) cooperative agreements with state, local, and tribal health departments&nbsp;to increase capacity for preventing and responding to vector-borne diseases.</p>","updateDate":"2026-07-16T21:39:21Z","versionCode":"07"}],"title":"To reauthorize the Kay Hagan Tick Act, and for other purposes.","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-09-19T23:40:54Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-09-19T23:40:54Z"}
